during the latter half of the 1990s one  of hollywood's biggest emerging stars  was none other than brendan fraser the  american canadian actor originally  gained widespread appeal through  comedies like encino man and george of  the jungle his biggest hit however came  in the form of a soft remake of a  classic 1932 horror film 1999's the  mummy starring frasier as american  adventurer rick o'connell the mummy went  on to gross over 155 million dollars  worldwide sparking a franchise that  would spawn two sequels a spin-off film  series and an animated show over the  next 10 years both sequels the mummy  returns and the mummy tomb of the dragon  emperor managed to rake in far more than  their predecessors despite this string  of great successes as a leading man  frasier would soon fade from the public  eye he worked consistently for a few  years after tomb of the dragon emperor  was released though not in anything with  the same widespread appeal as the mummy  franchise and then he seemed to  disappear entirely between 2015 and 2017  frasier seemingly swore off film  altogether and only appeared in a  handful of smaller scale tv roles as it  turns out a major factor in fraser's  disappearance from show business during  this time had to do with the mummy tomb  of the dragon emperor and its  predecessors in the mummy series he  later revealed that the franchise ended  up doing some serious damage to his  acting career literally in an interview  with gq in 2018 frasier candidly  revealed one of the things that caused  his hollywood hiatus essentially he was  at the end of his rope from over  exertion and injuries by the time i did  the third mummy picture in china i was  put together with tape and ice screw cap  ice packs and downhill mountain biking  pads cause they're small and light and  they can fit under your clothes i was  building an exoskeleton for myself daily  frazier was often his own stunt man and  injuries were not uncommon for the actor  he eventually needed to have surgery and  sometimes even those didn't go as  planned as frasier recalled i needed a  laminectomy and the lumbar didn't take  so they had to do it again a year later  while it might not have been the mummy  tomb of the dragon emperor that directly  caused all of these injuries it was the  film that amplified them and caused  frasier to slow down frazier also had a  partial knee replacement and lots of  painful work done on his back  additionally the actor needed to have  his vocal cords worked on frazier  remembered being in and out of hospitals  for just under seven years he was broken  and exhausted and enough was enough  in a sad comparison frazier compared  himself to a george orwell character i  felt like the horse from animal farm  whose job it was to work and work and  work orwell wrote a character who was i  think the proletariat he worked for the  good of the whole he didn't ask  questions he didn't make trouble until  it killed him  thankfully fraser has opted to slow down  a bit following this era of rest and  recovery his biggest breadwinner at the  moment doom patrol involves considerably  less physical risk for the 52 year old  even so he manages to bring much of the  personality that helped make him such an  effective leading man big things  continue to happen for the beloved actor  as he's recently been cast in martin  scorsese's killers of the flower moon  frazier will star alongside robert de  niro and leonardo dicaprio two actors he  hasn't had the pleasure of working with  yet additionally he is slated to appear  in brothers which is an upcoming comedy  film from legendary pictures after  showing fans that he's still got it in  steven soderbergh's recent flick no  sudden move supporters of frasier are  more than ecstatic to see him back in  the limelight we couldn't be more  excited for him check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about your favorite actors  are coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

